    "description": "Warren County Solar Project is a contracted solar project located on land owned by the Cincinnati Zoo in Warren County, Ohio. Its revenue base is tied to contracted electricity sales under two power-purchase agreements in the PJM market. The asset follows an asset-heavy and contracted renewable-infrastructure model based on project ownership, tax-equity financing, and long-duration offtake arrangements. Harrison Street’s announcement described the project at 28 MW, noted that it was acquired from Soltage, and stated that the site uses agrivoltaic sheep grazing for vegetation management. Harrison Street acquired the project in November 2022 through its social-infrastructure strategy; the ownership split is not publicly disclosed. The investment marked Harrison Street’s second infrastructure investment in the Cincinnati market after CoolCo.",
